yjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T22:17:56Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T22:17:56Z","body":"Thanks! I guess we need to figure out now why this particular HDRI behaves so much worse in 4.6. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3881041657/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3881106748","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116146#issuecomment-3881106748","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116146","id":3881106748,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nVP08","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T22:36:28Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T22:39:12Z","body":"As a temporary workaround, you can set `rendering/reflections/reflection_atlas/reflection_size` to 128. \n\nI have a feeling that the difference is explained by the slightly different sampling positions in the new approach. This HDRI is veeeeeery misbehaved. It has 2 pixels with color values that are over 20,000, while the rest of the image never goes above 250. That is absolutely the worse case scenario for IBL. \n\n_Edit: ahhhh, ya, that's it. Both 4.5 and 4.6 handle this sky really poorly, but 4.5 does a better job handling a fully rough dielectric since it smooths things out a bit more_\n\n_4.5.1_\n<img width=\"597\" height=\"541\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/36a0253f-3171-4191-b037-bd073e33dd25\" />\n\n_4.6-stable_\n<img width=\"597\" height=\"541\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/86460c08-dd37-4945-b93e-236fe2685e9c\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3881106748/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3881129551","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116146#issuecomment-3881129551","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116146","id":3881129551,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nVVZP","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T22:43:38Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T23:14:14Z","body":"~At any rate, this will be fixed by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108127~\n\n~To be clear, there are 4 possible solutions here:~\n~1. Make the `hdr_clamp_exposure` project setting enabled by default and make it more aggressive. This solves the problem at its source. Gamedevs love to download poorly formatted HDRIs and drop them directly into the engine. This option makes the HDRIs slightly better such that Godot can handle them.~\n~2. Increase the number of GGX samples in `rendering/reflections/sky_reflections/ggx_samples`. This is not a great solution since it has an exponential performance cost~\n~3. Modify our current Octahedral environment maps to handle this case better (I suspect adding a couple mip levels would help in this case). This isn't a great option since it would make sky more expensive on mobile (closer to the cost in 4.5) and doesn't address the root of the problem, it just hides the issue a bit (but as you can see above, the results with that HDRI are pretty shitty even in 4.5.1).~\n~4. Use SH for ambient light from the sky. SH are always smooth and hide the undersampling artifacts much better.~\n\n_Edit: After all that explaining, I found a much simpler fix lol. Will PR right away_","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3881129551/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3881263956","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116146#issuecomment-3881263956","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116146","id":3881263956,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nV2NU","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T23:25:56Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T23:31:30Z","body":"> > [@matheusmdx](https://github.com/matheusmdx) it is almost definitely from the octahedral PR you might want to start just by checking either side of it\n> \n> Luckily that was my first guess to revert and you're correct, reverting PR [#114908](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114908) fixes the issue.\n\nNot quite. the artifact just moves around with that PR\n\n_master with [#114908](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114908) reverted_\n<img width=\"597\" height=\"541\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a060e23e-dce4-4934-8fda-d8410dd2a39f\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3881263956/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3882324314","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116146#issuecomment-3882324314","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116146","id":3882324314,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nZ5Fa","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T05:51:12Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T05:51:12Z","body":"> This HDRI is veeeeeery misbehaved\n\nThe HDRI exaggerates the issue, but I first noticed this issue in a regular scene with the default godot physical sky shader and just a little bit of geometry around. If you have enough contrast in the scene it becomes noticeably noisier:\n\n| 4.5 | 4.6 |\n|--------|--------|\n| ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1b41f3d3-79dc-43d2-8b31-a0471aff0b1c) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c08d17b8-afbb-4388-8156-da2bdac68b25) |\n\nThe noise also varies a lot with the exact position of the probe, making it trickier to get good light from the main scene probe. Having smooth ambient light makes a big difference for clean dielectric surfaces\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d5469947-93b7-4248-93b0-631879dd69ff\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3882324314/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3951654076","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116146#issuecomment-3951654076","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116146","id":3951654076,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7riXS8","user":{"login":"SNAKFRIEN","id":65283327,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MjgzMzI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65283327?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN","html_url":"https://github.com/SNAKFRIEN","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SNAKFRIEN/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api